course: dictionary
lesson: 8362
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists each meaning separately, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word, because they are its context.
explain: «And Kieran swears rottweilers are killers, until he meets Maddie's neighbour's rottweiler, owner there, and it flops on its back for a belly rub.» Here a rottweiler is an animal, because it flops on its back and has a belly rub. Kieran's view that they are killers is proved wrong by the friendly dog.
explain: Rottweiler can also describe a person. If someone is called a rottweiler, they are fierce and aggressive when arguing or defending something. Ask yourself: is this a real animal, or a person acting in a fierce way? The clues tell you which.
fact: A Rottweiler is a large, strong breed of dog, black with brown markings.
fact: The breed was first bred in Germany to herd cattle and to guard.
fact: The breed is named after the German town of Rottweil.
fact: Rottweilers are loyal and protective but powerful, so always ask the owner before stroking any dog.
fact: Calling someone a rottweiler is informal, and it means they are fierce and aggressive in arguing or defending something.
exercise: «And Kieran swears rottweilers are killers, until he meets Maddie's neighbour's rottweiler, owner there, and it flops on its back for a belly rub.» What is the rottweiler in this sentence? | A kind teacher | A fierce person in an argument | A tiny cat | *A large dog
exercise: The lawyer was a rottweiler in court, never letting go of a point. What does rottweiler mean here? | Very sleepy and calm | *Fierce and aggressive when arguing | A large, black dog with brown markings | Kind and gentle to everyone
exercise: The breed is named after which place? | *The German town of Rottweil | The island of Skye | The town of Paris | The city of London
test: «Maddie's neighbour's rottweiler flopped on its back for a belly rub.» Before you stroke any dog, what should you do? | Shout at it loudly | Run away quickly | Pull its tail to say hello | *Ask the owner first
test: Mum says, «Don't argue with Dad, he's a rottweiler when he defends his garden.» What does rottweiler mean here? | A large, strong dog | *Fierce and aggressive when defending something | Very quiet and shy | Loyal to the family dog
exam: In the sentence «it flops on its back for a belly rub», which clue shows that rottweiler means a dog? | Kieran swears they are killers | Maddie is the neighbour | The word is a noun | *It flops on its back and has a belly rub
